SERVER NETWORK LATENCY ANALYSIS USING
DIJKSTRA'S ALGORITHM IN C++
PROBLEM STATEMENT
In computer networks, multiple servers are connected through network links, and
each link has a specific latency. Latency represents the time taken for data to travel
between connected servers. Identifying the minimum-latency paths is important for
efficient communication and network routing.
The purpose of this project is to develop a C++ program that represents servers as
vertices and network links as weighted edges in a graph, where each edge weight
represents latency. The program applies Dijkstra's Algorithm from a selected
source server to calculate the minimum latency to every reachable server. It then
ranks the reachable servers in ascending order of minimum latency and identifies
any servers that cannot be reached from the selected source.
